  "script": "The Mercedes AMG GT Coupe impresses with its diamond-patterned grille and bold front bumper, creating a look that screams performance from every angle. Born from Mercedes' illustrious racing heritage, the AMG GT embodies the brand's DNA, honing its prowess on tracks around the world. Under the hood, it packs a 4.0-liter twin-turbo V8 delivering a thrilling 469 horsepower and 465 lb-ft of torque, blending raw power with engineering brilliance. Its side profile reveals flared wheel arches that house striking black multi-spoke wheels, providing a dynamic and aggressive stance that\u2019s hard to ignore. The rear is dominated by a bold black wing that\u2019s not just for show\u2014it ensures aerodynamic stability at high speeds. Inside, the GT Coupe features a sleek center console with a touchpad, harmoniously integrating controls in a driver-focused cockpit. Priced around $115,000 when new, the GT Coupe now trades for about $75,000, that's around a 7% annual depreciation\u2014quite the deal for a performance beast. With its undeniable road presence and power, would the AMG GT be your pick for a thrilling drive?",
